From 0f2638e0c44ffff683cbf7621cb2ca0fc03727d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 23:37:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] sanitizers: numeric/bool casts (int)/(float)/(bool) are
 taint barriers (generic)

The cast SYNTAX was treated as an ordinary taint-propagating expression, so
(int) $_GET['id'] concatenated into SQL stayed tainted - a false positive on the
pervasive PHP-CMS pattern `Db::...('... = ' . (int)$x)`. Add NumericCastSanitizer
(int/integer/float/double/real/bool/boolean), complementing the intval/floatval/
settype/absint function sanitizers. Micro-test: (int)$x in SQL no longer flagged,
raw $x still flagged. bench recall unchanged (183/232). Generic, all PHP.
---
 php/ql/lib/codeql/php/security/FlowSources.qll | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/php/ql/lib/codeql/php/security/FlowSources.qll b/php/ql/lib/codeql/php/security/FlowSources.qll
index 21898d514fb..90685d5f0db 100644
--- a/php/ql/lib/codeql/php/security/FlowSources.qll
+++ b/php/ql/lib/codeql/php/security/FlowSources.qll
@@ -814,3 +814,21 @@ private class BuiltinSanitizer extends Sanitizer {
 private class GuardBarrier extends Sanitizer {
   GuardBarrier() { isGuardedRead(this) }
 }
+
+/**
+ * A value produced by a cast to a numeric or boolean type — `(int)`, `(integer)`, `(float)`,
+ * `(double)`, `(real)`, `(bool)`, `(boolean)`. Such a value cannot carry an injection / XSS / path /
+ * command payload, so it is a barrier for every taint class. This is generic to all PHP (every CMS
+ * casts request-supplied ids with `(int) $x` before using them in SQL) and complements the
+ * `intval` / `floatval` / `settype` / `absint` FUNCTION sanitizers — the cast SYNTAX was previously
+ * treated as an ordinary taint-propagating expression. `(string)` / `(binary)` / `(array)` casts still
+ * propagate, as before.
+ */
+private class NumericCastSanitizer extends Sanitizer {
+  NumericCastSanitizer() {
+    exists(CastExpr c |
+      c.getTypeName() = ["int", "integer", "float", "double", "real", "bool", "boolean"] and
+      this.asExpr() = c
+    )
+  }
+}
-- 
2.43.0


From 8e1a8574af2f1ed7e483eac012b76d277a3f8eed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 00:14:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] dataflow: apply the name-arity gate to
 first-class-callable method resolution

Consistency: the last name-only method-resolution site ($obj->m(...) first-class
callables) now uses the same nameFallbackAcceptable gate as viableCallable and
resolvesToCallee. Reuses the helper already bench-validated at the other two
sites (183/232); FCC method syntax is rare, so impact is small but the rule is
now applied uniformly.
---
 php/ql/lib/codeql/php/dataflow/internal/DataFlowPrivate.qll | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/php/ql/lib/codeql/php/dataflow/internal/DataFlowPrivate.qll b/php/ql/lib/codeql/php/dataflow/internal/DataFlowPrivate.qll
index 608774a4003..232a90134fc 100644
--- a/php/ql/lib/codeql/php/dataflow/internal/DataFlowPrivate.qll
+++ b/php/ql/lib/codeql/php/dataflow/internal/DataFlowPrivate.qll
@@ -807,7 +807,9 @@ predicate lambdaCreation(Node creation, LambdaCallKind kind, DataFlowCallable c)
       (
         c = TI::inferredMethod(mc)
         or
-        not TI::hasInferredReceiver(mc) and c.getName() = mc.getMethodName()
+        not TI::hasInferredReceiver(mc) and
+        c.getName() = mc.getMethodName() and
+        nameFallbackAcceptable(mc.getMethodName())
       )
     )
     or
